{"name":"Jean Jacket Blue","hex":"#7b90a2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jean","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Denim."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jean"},{"term":"jacket","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of certain types of outerwear.\nA piece of clothing worn on the upper body outside a shirt or blouse, often waist length to thigh length.\nA piece of a person's suit, beside trousers and, sometimes, waistcoat; coat .\nAn outer garment (usually white) intended for chefs and which may be taken to signify status.\n A vest ; a waistcoat .\n A letter jacket.","A piece of clothing worn on the upper body outside a shirt or blouse, often waist length to thigh length."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To confine (someone) to a straitjacket. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To enclose or encase in a jacket or other covering."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jacket"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jean jacket","blocks":[{"text":"A denim jacket, also called a jean jacket, jeans jacket or trucker jacket, is a jacket made from denim. Introduced in the United States in the late 19th century, it has been a popular type of casual apparel with both men and women and has been described as an iconic element of American fashion. Though a staple of western wear, the denim jacket has also enjoyed a more general appeal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Riga-12_moped._Fortepan_6735.jpg/330px-Riga-12_moped._Fortepan_6735.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean_jacket","wikidata":"Q48524668"},{"title":"Jacket","blocks":[{"text":"A jacket is a garment for the upper body, usually extending below the hips. A jacket typically has long or short sleeves and fastens in the front or slightly on the side. Jackets without sleeves are vests. A jacket is generally lighter, tighter-fitting, and less insulating than a coat, but both are outerwear. Some jackets are fashionable, while some others serve as protective clothing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Jacket2-1.jpg/330px-Jacket2-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacket","wikidata":"Q849964"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Denim_Jacket_%2851079649933%29.jpg/500px-Denim_Jacket_%2851079649933%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Denim_Jacket_%2851079649933%29.jpg/1280px-Denim_Jacket_%2851079649933%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Denim_Jacket_%2851079649933%29.jpg/500px-Denim_Jacket_%2851079649933%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Levi Strauss Type III jacket","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADenim_Jacket_(51079649933).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Canadian_tuxedo.jpg/500px-Canadian_tuxedo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Canadian_tuxedo.jpg/1280px-Canadian_tuxedo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Canadian_tuxedo.jpg/500px-Canadian_tuxedo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A man sitting on a statue of a tortoise and wearing a Canadian tuxedo","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACanadian_tuxedo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Reagan_with_horse.jpg/120px-Reagan_with_horse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Reagan_with_horse.jpg/250px-Reagan_with_horse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Reagan_with_horse.jpg/120px-Reagan_with_horse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AReagan_with_horse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Denim_jacket.jpg/120px-Denim_jacket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte